@bank all
// Pillar 5 Step 3 (head writer W2): texts said by nobody, for the test job and the first promotion (seat C2), team
// jobs (M2), tracing (M3), the T2 band, P1 and P2 (H2), the bridge lock and the turn-in meters (C2, U). Keys in
// content/works/keys-p5.md, "Step 3". Mails are "Subject | body", unsigned (the game adds the sender).

// ---- the ladder rows
== works.mech.m8
- team jobs
== works.mech.m9
- tracing
== works.mech.p1
- when does it happen?
== works.mech.p2
- who saw what?

// ---- the test job and the first promotion (C2)
// C2's keys (worksText): Calder's words in the bay, Day 8
== promo.announce
- Tomorrow, your test job. Tier 2, a real one. I'll follow. I won't help. Sleep tonight.
// ... by Mail, if you're not in the bay by 10:00 (Calder sends it)
== promo.announce.mail
- Your test job | Tomorrow, your test job. A real Tier 2 job. I'll be watching. Sleep.
// Calder as the test job goes up, 09:00 Day 9
== promo.test.start
- There it is. Yours. I'm watching, not helping.
// passed: the scrubber's put right
== promo.test.passed
- Filter in, fan settled. That'll do. Go and have your tea.
// not done: another in two work days ({day}: the weekday)
== promo.test.again
- Not done isn't failed. Another on {day}. Get a few more filters under your belt.
// Day 10, 10:30: the urgent toast, and Torres's nudge
== promo.summons
- Chief Calder: My office, 11:00. — C.
== promo.summons.torres
- Go on. She doesn't bite. Usually.
// the office scene's words by Mail, if you never came (Calder sends it)
== promo.mail
- Your promotion | You weren't about, so you'll read it instead. You passed. As of today you're an Officer: Technician, Tier 2. Your badge and your pip are on my desk; collect them. You move to cabin 4-23 tonight. The Captain commissions you tomorrow at 17:15. Clean uniform. Well done.
// the Record's milestones and the keepsake
== works.ms.officer
- Promoted to Officer, day {n}.
== works.ms.commissioned
- Commissioned Officer, day {n}.
== works.keepsake.commission
- Your commission, framed. The Captain's signature is very neat.
// the door plate of 4-23
== works.plate
- {name} · {rank}
// the Captain's Mail on Day 10 (Mail, up to 400)
== promo.captain
- Congratulations | Chief Calder tells me you've earned your pip. Well done. The ceremony is tomorrow at 17:15, in the observation room on Deck 1. Bring one honest answer: what should an officer never forget? I'll ask.
// Day 11, morning: from the Captain's office
== mail.promo.ceremony
- Your commission, 17:15 | The officer ceremony is today at 17:15, observation room, Deck 1. Clean uniform. It takes ten minutes. There will be tea.
// the move, if you were asleep or away (Calder's words by Mail)
== mail.promo.move
- Your cabin | You weren't about, so we moved you anyway. Cabin 4-23, officers' corridor. Your things are there. Your key opens it. Quiet hours after 23:00. Your door's your own now: use it. Tomas says don't be a stranger.
// the Ship app's news item (one gossip line)
== promo.news
- Works news: {me} made Officer today. Cake at the tea corner, while it lasts.

// ---- what's next: see next.lines

// ---- the bridge (C2; DA5's tap hook)
== bridge.locked
- The bridge. You need the Captain's permission to go in.
- Bridge crew only, for now. The Captain invites you in, in time.
// the invitation itself is Vance's meeting bridgeInvite (content/meetings/bridgeInvite.meet)

// ---- the turn-in (C2, U)
== works.turnin.rep
- Works reputation up
== works.turnin.meter
- +{n} {system}
== works.turnin.repN
- +{n} {dept} reputation
== meter.air
- Air
== meter.water
- Water
== meter.power
- Power
== meter.heat
- Heat
== meter.food
- Food
== meter.waste
- Waste & laundry
== meter.hull
- Hull
== meter.comms
- Comms & sensors
== meter.propulsion
- Propulsion
== meter.transport
- Lift & doors

// ---- team jobs (M2)
== works.ask.m8
- Recycler, 09:30 | Recycler's membrane bank, 09:30, Deck 3. Need four. You're the fourth. — E.H.
== team.name.recycler
- Recycler membrane change
== team.name.washer
- Washer overhaul
== team.name.manifold
- Manifold valve bank
== team.name.heater
- Heating pump swap
== team.name.scrubber
- Scrubber fan change
// the board card
== team.card
- {job}, {time}, Deck {deck}. A team of {n}.
// the 16:00 Mail the day before
== mail.team
- Team job, {time} | {job} tomorrow at {time}, Deck {deck}. {name} leads. You're on the team: be at your spot when it starts.
// your turn (a toast)
== team.turn.brace
- Your turn: brace the housing
== team.turn.pass
- Your turn: pass the new part
== team.turn.hold
- Your turn: hold it steady
== team.turn.crank
- Your turn: crank the drum
== team.turn.tip
- Your turn: tip it and hold
== team.turn.valves
- Your turn: close the valves, in order
== team.turn.open
- Your turn: open the valves again
== team.turn.drain
- Your turn: drain it down
== team.start
- The team's here. Find your spot.
== team.wait
- {name}'s team is waiting for you. Your spot's free.
== team.late
- {name} started without you. They'll manage. Slower.
== team.done
- Team job done. Good work, all of you.

// ---- tracing (M3)
== works.ask.m9
- The pipe kit | Board, first thing. Showers on Four are weak. You'll find out why.
== trace.title
- Pipe kit · {machine}
== trace.full
- full
== trace.low
- low
== trace.verylow
- very low
== trace.before
- Before: {word}
== trace.after
- After: {word}
== trace.found
- Full before, low after. It's {machine}.
== trace.wrongline
- Not on this line.
== trace.symptom.water
- Showers weak on Deck {deck}
== trace.symptom.heat
- Cold cabins on Deck {deck}
== trace.symptom.air
- Stuffy air on Deck {deck}
== trace.line.water
- the water line
== trace.line.heat
- the heat line
== trace.line.air
- the air line
== chief.m9.1
- Read the middle first. Halve the line each time.
== chief.m9.2
- Fine before, low after: that's your machine. A walk is cheaper than a guess.

// ---- head-scratchers: T2, P1, P2 (H2)
== case.wrong.t2
- Not that. The {part} is spent, but now you know.
== chief.p1.1
- Bad all day: something's worn. Bad at the busy hours: something can't keep up.
== chief.p1.2
- Read the logs. A part that's fine in the morning can't be bad all day.
== case.title.p1
- {machine} {shows}, but only {when}.
== case.when.evening
- in the evening
== case.when.morning
- in the morning
== case.when.night
- at night
== case.when.peak
- at the busy hours
== case.when.after
- after it's been used
== case.strip.title
- {machine}'s log
== case.strip.fine
- Fine {from}-{to}
== case.strip.low
- Low {from}-{to}
== chief.p2.1
- Ask who was there, and check they were.
== chief.p2.2
- Nobody lies. Somebody's mixed up. The Roster knows which.
== case.ask
- Ask about the fault
// P1's card: the end of the line, and what it does (H2 fills {deck})
== case.line.water
- Showers on Deck {deck}
== case.line.heat
- Cabins on Deck {deck}
== case.line.air
- The air on Deck {deck}
== case.line.water.shows
- run weak
== case.line.heat.shows
- run cold
== case.line.air.shows
- is stuffy

// ---- the Tiles game (U): a small line under the score (U adds the pause sign)
== tiles.paused
- The ship's clock is paused while you play
